    <bpmn:process id="W_W5545" name="W5545. BIR Tax-Enforcement Suspension &amp; Closure-Order Response (Oplan Kandado)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BIR serves a tax-enforcement suspension or closure order against a BuildRight store, branch, or registered seat — the Oplan Kandado class (preliminary 5-day closure for survey/inventory verification, or suspension of business for verified under-declaration under the RR/RMC closure framework) — or an LOA/audit escalation signals imminent enforcement closure
Frequency: Rare; realistically 0–2 enforcement events per decade chain-wide; audit-risk-weighted sites are the exposure surface
Volume: 1 order × 1+ closed site (trading halt at that site — the PHP 840K/day per-store downtime canon) × statutory reinstatement mechanics × 5-entity registration structure
Owner: Tax Manager
Participants: CFO, VP Legal, BIR-accredited tax counsel, Finance Controller, Regional Manager &amp; Store Manager (closure/reopening execution), Corporate Secretary (protests &amp; records), Compliance (VS-22 regulatory-desk linkage), HR (site-staff continuity), IR if material (W5019)
Source: workflow W5545 — BIR Tax-Enforcement Suspension &amp; Closure-Order Response (Oplan Kandado)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5545_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5545_Lane1" name="Tax Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5545_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5545_Lane3" name="Tax Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5545_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5545_Start5" name="BIR serves a tax-enforcement suspension or closure order against a BuildRight store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task6" name="Order intake &amp; verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Order intake &amp; verification: Tax Manager receives the served order; verify authenticity and legal basis (issuing RDO, provision cited — survey closure vs under-declaration suspension, scope: which TIN/branch codes and premises, effective time and duration); confirm immediate compliance duty with counsel; notify CFO and the Regional Manager of the affected site
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: &lt; 2 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task7" name="Site closure execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Site closure execution: the affected site executes closure mechanics per W850 (cash securing, systems sign-out, signage per the order&#x27;s terms — no voluntary scope expansion beyond what the order covers); staff deployment handled (redeployment to nearby sites or paid stand-by per HR); inventory and books at the site preserved for the survey/verification if ordered
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task8" name="Legal assessment &amp; protest track">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Legal assessment &amp; protest track: counsel assesses the cited violation against the site&#x27;s documented compliance (registered invoices/CRM, VAT returns, books); file the appropriate protest/reconsideration within the statutory window; where the violation is verified, negotiate settlement/compromise per the W2773 controversy-governance framework — resolution speed is the revenue lever
Responsible (R): Tax Counsel / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Days–weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task9" name="Remediation &amp; reinstatement package">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Remediation &amp; reinstatement package: correct the underlying defect chain-wide-relevant (invoicing configuration, unreported receipts, books); assemble compliance evidence (updated returns, payment proofs, ATP/registration records); present to the issuing RDO and secure the lifting/reinstatement order in writing
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task10" name="Reopening execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reopening execution: on receipt of the lifting order, the site reopens per W850 mechanics; revenue-recovery steps (promo, local outreach) per store practice; spoilage/damage and inventory variances from the closed window reconciled (W64 seasonal exposure where relevant)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: &lt; 24 h after lifting</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task11" name="Chain-wide prevention sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Chain-wide prevention sweep: audit the violated obligation across all sites and entities (same invoice/receipt configuration, same filing posture); register-level compliance checklist updated; the event feeds the W2776 tax risk register with root cause and detection gap
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / Tax Specialists
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5545_Task12" name="Governance &amp; disclosure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Governance &amp; disclosure: penalty/settlement accrual posted and financial-statement impact assessed per W590/W2775; Audit Committee briefed; if the event is material to a listed company, IR runs the W5017/W5019 disclosure assessment
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO / Audit Committee
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5545_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5545_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5545_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5545_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-468 (ensure controlled execution — Corporate Income Tax, Local Tax, DST &amp; BIR Audit Defense (PA-79.3).) | - operational: no site reopens without the written BIR lifting order on file — W850&#x27;s trading judgment never substitutes for the regulator&#x27;s order | - operational: every closure-order event closes with a chain-wide compliance sweep result recorded in the W2776 register
Owner: Tax Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5545_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5545_Annotation14" targetRef="W5545_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow16" sourceRef="W5545_Start5" targetRef="W5545_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow17" sourceRef="W5545_Task6" targetRef="W5545_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow18" sourceRef="W5545_Task7" targetRef="W5545_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow19" sourceRef="W5545_Task8" targetRef="W5545_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow20" sourceRef="W5545_Task9" targetRef="W5545_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow21" sourceRef="W5545_Task10" targetRef="W5545_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow22" sourceRef="W5545_Task11" targetRef="W5545_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5545_Flow23" sourceRef="W5545_Task12" targetRef="W5545_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
